      "message": "### Adjectives as variable names (`done`)\n\n**Location:** `bootrom.cc` (`BackupFlash` and `ProgramRawCommandPayload`)\n\n**The Issue:**\n\n```cpp\nuint32_t done \u003d flash_addr - bootrom_protocol::kFlashBaseAddr;\nPrintProgress(\"Backup Progress\", done, total_size);\n\n```\n\n\"Done\" is an adjective, which makes it a great name for a boolean flag (`bool is_done \u003d false;`), but a terrible name for an integer counter.\n\n**The Fix:**\nRename it to `bytes_processed`, `bytes_read`, or `bytes_written` depending on the context.",
