      "message": "### `status` vs `result` for Monads\n\n**Location:** `et171_flash.cc` (inside `main()`)\n\n**The Issue:**\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, egis::AppError\u003e status;\nif (config.mode \u003d\u003d egis::AppMode::kFlashFw) {\n  status \u003d egis::ExecuteFirmwareFlash(config, bootrom_comm);\n}\n\n```\n\n\"Status\" usually implies a primitive integer or an enum (like the `uint16_t status` inside your `SecureResponseHeader`). A `std::expected` is fundamentally a functional Result monad (representing either Success or an Error).\n\n**The Fix:**\nRename `status` to `result` or `flash_result` to align with standard C++23 functional nomenclature.",
