      "side": 1,
      "message": "### The `_opt` suffix on a Vector\n\n**Location:** `file_util.cc` (`LoadAesKey`)\n\n**The Issue:**\n\n```cpp\nauto key_res \u003d ReadBinaryFile(key_file_path);\n// ...\nauto \u0026key_opt \u003d *key_res;\n\n```\n\nBecause `key_res` is a `std::expected`, dereferencing it yields the inner `std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e`. Naming it `key_opt` is highly misleading because, in modern C++, the `_opt` suffix is universally understood to mean `std::optional`. A reader scanning this code will assume they need to check `if (key_opt.has_value())`, which isn\u0027t true here.\n\n**The Fix:**\nRename it to reflect its actual type: `key_data` or `raw_key_bytes`.",
